#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:295
msgid "The \"Ready When You Are\" call-to-action - the eyebrow, heading, body text and two button labels for the banner near the bottom of every yacht details page. Use {yacht_name} in the heading or text to insert that yacht's name automatically. A yacht can override this wording entirely from its own Review & Publish step; what you set here is just the fallback for yachts that don't bother to."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:305
msgid "This is a two-step decision: which payment flow you use, then which method(s) inside that flow are switched on."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:312
msgid "The Settings: Payments tab, showing the Custom Payment Methods vs WooCommerce Checkout flow cards, a \"You're configuring\" banner, and the Offline, PayPal and Stripe method cards each with an enable toggle and a Configure link."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:313
msgid "Settings → Payments, configured for Custom Payment Methods with Offline, PayPal and Stripe all enabled."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:316
msgid "Step 1 - the flow"
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:318
msgid "Two cards, exactly one selected at a time - click a card to switch. The \"You're configuring:\" banner underneath always confirms which one is currently active, so the fields below it are never ambiguous."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:327
msgid "Offline, PayPal, and Stripe, run directly by this plugin - no WooCommerce needed."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:332
msgid "Bookings go through WooCommerce's own cart, checkout, and orders instead. If WooCommerce isn't active yet, this card shows its own \"Install & Activate WooCommerce\" button - clicking it installs, activates, and switches you into this flow in one step."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:336
msgid "These two are mutually exclusive on purpose - a booking is only ever paid for one way, so switching flows resets the other side rather than risk both trying to handle the same booking."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:342
msgid "Step 2 - the methods"
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:343
msgid "If you picked Custom Payment Methods:"
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:347
msgid "Method"
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:348
msgid "What its fields do"
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:354
msgid "No API keys - just an \"Instructions\" note the guest sees at checkout (e.g. how to pay by bank transfer). Good default while you're setting everything else up."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:358
msgid "Your PayPal email, and Sandbox (testing, no real money moves) or Live."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:362
msgid "Publishable Key and Secret Key from your Stripe Dashboard, plus a Webhook Secret if you've set up a Stripe webhook for this site. Once a key is saved, its field shows a note instead of the key itself - leave it blank to keep the saved one."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:367
msgid "Each method is a card: the switch enables/disables it, the badge shows its current state, and \"Configure\" opens its fields without needing it switched on first - handy for filling in Stripe keys ahead of time, then flipping it on when you're ready. Turning a method on also opens its fields automatically, since that's usually exactly why you turned it on. Whichever methods are enabled populate the \"Default Payment Method\" dropdown at the bottom - that's what a guest sees pre-selected at checkout."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:372
msgid "If you picked WooCommerce Checkout:"
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:374
msgid "A \"WooCommerce Payment Methods\" panel lists every gateway WooCommerce itself knows about (Cash on Delivery, Direct Bank Transfer, plus anything a WooCommerce extension you've installed adds) with the same quick switch and status badge. Flipping one here is the same as flipping it in WooCommerce's own Settings → Payments screen - they read and write the exact same option. For a gateway's own detailed settings (API keys, instructions, fees), use the \"Open in WooCommerce\" link, which takes you straight to WooCommerce's native settings for it."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:383
msgid "Off-days and simple across-the-fleet pricing adjustments, applied to every yacht unless a yacht-specific rule is added later. Add as many rules as you need with \"+ Add Rule\" - each one is a label, a type, and a from/to date range. Three types:"
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:390
msgid "The Settings: Pricing Rules tab, showing an empty rule row with Label, Type, From Date and To Date fields and an \"+ Add Rule\" button."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:391
msgid "Settings → Pricing Rules: fleet-wide off-days and weekday/seasonal price adjustments."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:394
msgid "Off-Day"
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:394
msgid "blocks a date (or date range) from being booked at all - a maintenance day, a public holiday, a private event."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:395
msgid "Weekday/Weekend"
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:395
msgid "a percent or fixed-amount adjustment for particular days of the week."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:396
msgid "the same kind of adjustment, but for a date range instead of a weekday - a summer peak-season surcharge, for example."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:402
msgid "Everything to do with the confirmation email a guest receives, and who it appears to come from."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:409
msgid "The Settings: Email tab, showing Sender Identity fields, a Confirmation Email subject and rich-text body editor with a \"Send Test Email\" button, a \"Send Confirmation On\" checklist of booking statuses, and a Dynamic Variables panel of clickable placeholders."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:410
msgid "Settings → Email: sender identity, the confirmation email template, and the dynamic variables it can insert."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:413
msgid "Sender Identity - the From name/address on confirmation emails. Leave either blank to fall back to your site name / admin email."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:414
msgid "Confirmation Email - the default subject and body sent when a booking is confirmed. Insert booking details (guest name, dates, total price, and so on) with the variable buttons on the right; \"Send Test Email\" lets you preview it in your own inbox before it goes near a real guest. A yacht can override this from its own Review & Publish step."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:415
msgid "Send Confirmation On - which booking status(es) trigger the email. Most sites want this to match whatever status their payment method marks a paid booking with."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:421
msgid "Two small switches that decide how long a guest's personal details stick around, and what happens to the plugin's data if it's ever removed."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:428
msgid "The Settings: Data & Privacy tab, showing an \"Anonymize guest data after (months)\" number field set to 0, and an unchecked \"Remove all plugin data when uninstalled\" checkbox."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:429
msgid "Settings → Data & Privacy: retention and uninstall behavior, both off by default."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:432
msgid "Anonymize guest data after (months) - guest name/email/phone on old bookings are scrubbed after this many months. Set to 0 to keep guest data indefinitely."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:433
msgid "Remove all plugin data when uninstalled - leave this off unless you're sure; switching it on means deleting the plugin also deletes every yacht, booking, and guest record it created."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:438
msgid "Three views of the same underlying bookings, each suited to a different question."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:441
msgid "The Bookings admin screen, a table listing each booking's yacht, guest, charter type, dates, duration, total, order and status, with a Delete action and an \"All Statuses\" filter."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:442
msgid "Bookings - every booking across the whole fleet, newest first, filterable by status."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:445
msgid "every booking made through any of the shortcodes above, in one flat list, with its status and payment state. \"Delete\" here removes the booking record itself - use it for test/duplicate bookings, not as a way to cancel a real one (change its status instead, so the guest's history stays intact)."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:446
msgid "the same bookings laid out by date, per yacht - the fastest way to see what's free this week or spot a scheduling clash before you confirm a new request."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:447
msgid "everyone who has ever booked, with their contact details and booking history in one place - this is the data the Data & Privacy retention setting eventually anonymizes once it's old enough."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:453
msgid "\"Book Now\" isn't clickable / no price shows: check that the yacht has at least one price set for the booking type being requested (Yachts → edit the yacht → Pricing & Availability), and that a payment method is enabled (Settings → Payments)."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:454
msgid "A yacht isn't showing up in the search or list shortcode: make sure it's Published, not a Draft, and that any Class/Occasion/location filter a visitor has selected actually matches it."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:455
msgid "Confirmation emails aren't arriving: use \"Send Test Email\" on Settings → Email first to rule out a hosting/SMTP problem, then check that \"Send Confirmation On\" includes the status your payment method actually sets."
msgstr ""

#: assets/admin/src/routes/UserGuide.js:456
msgid "Switched to WooCommerce Checkout and nothing is enabled: that's expected right after installing WooCommerce - open the \"WooCommerce Payment Methods\" panel and switch at least one gateway (Cash on Delivery is the quickest to test with) on."
msgstr ""

